---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="What 5 Minute Mandarin is, how the lessons work, and what it is not."
  path="/about/"
  nav="about"
>
  <div class="page-narrow">
  <h1>About 5 Minute Mandarin</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      5 Minute Mandarin brings Mandarin tutors and their students together in one place: lessons on a shared calendar,
      calls on Zoom, a group chat for each class and a private chat with your tutor.
    </p>
    <p>
      Between lessons there are free five-minute practice lessons for complete beginners. Five minutes a day does more
      than an hour once a week, so they are kept small on purpose.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="card" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <h2 id="how-title">How a practice lesson works</h2>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li>Learn: each word in Chinese characters, in pinyin (the spelling in Latin letters) and in English.</li>
      <li>Listen: if your device has a Mandarin voice installed, a Listen button says each word.</li>
      <li>Check: one question at a time. See the word, pick what it means.</li>
      <li>Take the check again whenever you like. Your best score is kept.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="pinyin-title">
    <h2 id="pinyin-title">Reading pinyin</h2>
    <p>
      The mark over a vowel is the tone: <span lang="zh-Latn-pinyin">ā</span> is high and level,
      <span lang="zh-Latn-pinyin">á</span> rises, <span lang="zh-Latn-pinyin">ǎ</span> dips and rises, and
      <span lang="zh-Latn-pinyin">à</span> falls. No mark means a short, light syllable. Lesson 1 covers this.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you are ready, turn off pinyin in the check from the <b>Aa</b> menu and read the characters on their own.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <h2 id="limits-title">What this is not</h2>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li>Not a full course. It is a first step, and a good one to take before a class, an app or a trip.</li>
      <li>
        Not yet reviewed. These lessons are first versions. They have not been checked by a Mandarin teacher, so if
        you spot a mistake, please say.
      </li>
      <li>
        Not a substitute for real voices. The Listen button uses your device's computer voice, which is a good guide
        but not perfect.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="fine">
      The lessons teach Mandarin as spoken in mainland China, written in simplified characters.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <h2 id="privacy-title">Your practice progress</h2>
    <p>
      Your practice progress and reading settings are saved in this browser only. Nothing is sent anywhere, there is no account
      and no tracking. The Listen button only uses voices installed on your device, so the words are not sent to a
      speech service either.
    </p>
    <button type="button" class="btn ghost block" data-clear hidden>Clear my progress</button>
    <p class="fine" data-cleared role="status" hidden>Your progress has been cleared.</p>
  </section>

  </div>

  <script>
    import { clearAll } from '../scripts/progress';

    const clear = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-clear]')!;
    const cleared = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-cleared]')!;
    clear.hidden = false;
    clear.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!confirm('Clear your progress in every lesson? This cannot be undone.')) return;
      clearAll();
      cleared.hidden = false;
    });
  </script>
</Base>
